  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "intro",
      "heading": "DnD 5.5 Shield Master Feat Guide | 2024 DnD",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-intro-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Thanks HEMA"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With the 2024 Rules update, DnD 5e’s Shield Master feat got some frankly huge quality of life updates at the cost of a feature that was hard to both remember how to use accurately and then, even when you did, it was hardly ever relevant. It’s all about focusing on the “and board” style of fighting and it has two very powerful features. We’re going to discuss the changes to the first feature and how it compares to other similar options, then talk about ways to make sure you’re optimizing both the Prone condition you inflict and the Reaction which the Feat grants."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "First (and, perhaps, foremost), because all non-origin feats grant +1 ability score increases in the 2024 rules, they are "
            },
            {
              "type": "emphasis",
              "text": "much"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " easier to slot into a build without getting too much off the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Fundamental Math",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/fundamental_math/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " than they were in the 2014 rules. While Shield Master only allows us to increase Strength, I can’t actually come up with an optimal build offhand that would want this feat and any other stat bonus early in the level progression. This immediately presents a huge usability boon before we start talking about features."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
